# reactullm-sdd ⇄ pyllum connection
# ---------------------------------
# Path to the shared planning contract (reactullm-pyllum.contract.json).
# This is the ONLY switch for the pyllum connection:
#
#   • set   → pyllum reads this contract and serves as reactullm-sdd's
#             request-mode planner backend.
#   • unset → the connection is OFF. reactullm-sdd falls back to its own
#             injected ChatClient (or plan mode, which needs no model at all).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and point it at the contract. An absolute path is
# safest since the two repos live in sibling directories.
#
# REACTULLM_PYLLUM_CONTRACT=/absolute/path/to/reactullm/reactullm-pyllum.contract.json

# Model pyllum uses when filling the TestPlan (any pyllum-supported model id).
# Only consulted when REACTULLM_PYLLUM_CONTRACT is set.
# REACTULLM_PYLLUM_MODEL=gpt-5.4


# Cross-stack HANDOFF (bidirectional API contract)
# ------------------------------------------------
# Shared directory holding the handoff contract that flows BOTH ways:
#   • backend-first  → pyllum/FastAPI generates, writes the API it exposes;
#                      reactullm consumes it and builds a matching front.
#   • frontend-first → reactullm generates, writes the data its components need;
#                      pyllum consumes it and builds a matching backend.
#
# The directory holds handoff.contract.json + HANDOFF_DONE.json + a run log.
# Each generation is stamped with a sortable runId; the consumer implements
# ONLY the latest completed run. Same switch discipline as above:
#
#   • set   → the handoff is active; both repos read/write this shared dir.
#   • unset → the handoff is OFF (no error).
#
# REACTULLM_PYLLUM_HANDOFF_DIR=/absolute/path/to/shared/handoff